 debt) funding a fast-rising CFR (to ~\u00a32.36bn by 2030/31).","gaps":[{"id":"PI-08","evidence":"TMSS p.11 / Report p.27: 'income funded debt servicing as % of net capital financing budget' 14.5% (limit 15%)"},{"id":"LB-04","evidence":""},{"id":"COM-02","evidence":"TMSS p.25 / CIS p.40-41 carry the substance of PC para 51 (no borrowing for yield)"},{"id":"COM-05","evidence":"CIS p.46-47: Financial Regulatory Framework, due diligence and monitoring for non-treasury loans"},{"id":"COM-07","evidence":"CIS p.46-47 fair-value disclosure in the accounts; income-funded-debt-servicing indicator 14.5% (TMSS p.11); CIS p.44-45 notes need for robust income if downturn"},{"id":"COM-08","evidence":"CIS p.48-49 asset-release categories 8-10 and capital-receipt disposal framework (property)"}],"documents":[{"title":"Treasury Management Strategy 2026/27 (Appendix 5 to the CSR Budget report; Cabinet 13 Feb 2026, recommended to Full Council 24 Feb 2026)","url":"https://democracy.cornwall.gov.uk/documents/s194666/Cornwall%20Council%20Comprehensive%20Spending%20Review%20Budget%20Proposals%20202627%20to%20202829%20-%20Appendix%205.pdf","fy":"2026/27"},{"title":"Capital and Investment Strategy 2026/27-2030/31 (Appendix 6)","url":"https://democracy.cornwall.gov.uk/documents/s194667/Cornwall%20Council%20Comprehensive%20Spending%20Review%20Budget%20Proposals%20202627%20to%20202829%20-%20Appendix%206.pdf","fy":"2026/27"},{"title":"Comprehensive Spending Review: Budget Proposals 2026/27 to 2028/29 (Cabinet/Council report - source for S151 statement, reserves, affordability indicators)","url":"https://democracy.cornwall.gov.uk/documents/s194661/Cornwall%20Council%20Comprehensive%20Spending%20Review%20Budget%20Proposals%20202627%20to%20202829%20-%20Report.pdf","fy":"2026/27"}]},"documents":[{"title":"20260917 - Pensions - Cornwall Pension Fund Update Investments Part 1 - Report - PUBLIC","url":"https://democracy.cornwall.gov.uk/documents/s200580/20260917-pensions-cornwall-pension-fund-update-